{
  "dom_id": "step-e2557",
  "name": "Example: Finding a Midpoint Using the Midpoint Formula",
  "problem": "Which number corresponds to the midpoint of the line segment $\\overline{AB}$ shown below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14171842/assets/8850f207b51c6789073a0fb83b221a93290ade40b3f148248cac803fc1486452.png)",
  "worked_solution": "The point $A$ corresponds to the number $x_1=-1$ while $B$ corresponds to $x_2=5.$ \n\nTo find the number $x_m$ corresponding to the midpoint $M$, we use the midpoint formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{m} & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1+5}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the midpoint $M$ corresponds to $x_m=2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14171842/assets/07d9c940fbe2e5a14c5dc3fc1b46add8947f9ad0df7151f8693793cf70359688.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
